        <ChangeNotes Value="v1.3.4 - THE MOD LOADS WITHOUT WAR SAILS AGAIN. If you don't own War Sails, versions 1.3.0 to 1.3.3 failed on startup with a dependency error and the mod never loaded at all - my mistake, and thank you to the player who reported it. One class inside the sea-scout code was tied to the DLC in a way that made the whole mod need it. It now lives in its own file that is only ever opened when War Sails is actually installed. Nothing changes for anyone who owns the DLC. If you were stuck on 1.2, this is the update to take." />
        <!-- previous release notes, kept for reference:
        <ChangeNotes Value="v1.3.3 - THE VILLAGE KEEPS ITS OWN GROUND. Fights near a village are fought inside that village - the game's own rule, which the mod used to ignore. Now: 'Select the battlefield' is closed there and names the village. The scout ride takes you INTO the village, instead of a field you would never fight on. Away from villages, nothing changes." />
        <ChangeNotes Value="v1.3.2 - THE GROUND ANSWERS AGAIN. Fixes, both from player reports. THE BATTLEFIELD PICKERS: a party standing in forest, hills or snow was offered no choice of ground at all - those lands carry no battlefields of their own in the game's data, so the list came up empty and both the 'select the battlefield' option and the scout's picker quietly vanished. The search now widens in steps: the ground you stand on first, then fields that merely have your terrain in them (a plain with a mountain in it is a real answer in the mountains), then kindred country - a forest fight offered the thickest woods the game owns, marked plainly when the field belongs to another land. Bandit hunts in the woods and hills have their choice of ground back. THE SCOUT RIDE: the lone ride out is a battlefield with no battle, and it carried no teams at all - which crashed other mission mods that reasonably assume every mission has sides (War Horns, reported on Nexus). The ride now sets up proper empty sides before you spawn. Nothing changes for the rider; other mods simply find what they expect." />
        <ChangeNotes Value="v1.3.0 - THE WALLS AND SAILS UPDATE. Two new drill grounds. CASTLES: at your own castle the muster becomes a SIEGE drill (its own option on the castle menu) - storm your own walls or hold them, on the castle's real scene at its true wall level. The garrison and militia stand with the defense, your ENGINEER's skill unlocks the siege equipment in tiers (both sides armed on your purse), a grand muster costs more, keeps a per-castle clock, and earns a little renown and influence. The mock enemy comes to the walls too - phantoms besiege you when you hold, reinforce the garrison when you storm. THE SEA (War Sails): divide the fleet AT YOUR WORD through the new ship-divide window (or let it follow the men - every hull comes home either way); the phantom SHIPYARD lays down the mock enemy's fleet, any culture's hulls, fitted as you please; and the scout ride SAILS - take the flagship out with your crew, no battle, no cost, hull home without a scratch. THE YARD: your STEWARD speeds the drill cooldown, and your best-fighting companions INSTRUCT, adding to the XP kept. Plus the fixes the playtests earned: the siege auto-resolve now truly fights on the walls, no post-battle menu can restart a drill or mint prisoners, and phantom casualties no longer inflate your own losses." />
